Z||000000||AOCM77||11-25-2001||10:55 AM||||Bought an 86 V-6 SE last year it has been a great car, drove from West coast to East coast and back. Well last week while driving 65 mph came to a stop and it would not down shift out of 4th, needless to say pushing in on the clutch pedal didn't help. The car then stalled and coasted to a stop, after stopping I was then able to down shift. Was told by a couple local repair shops it was the clutch. I am really confused cause it runs great now with no problem reoccurance. Also are there any repair manuals available to purchase? Thanks !||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||11-25-2001||11:13 AM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>From what you have described, it may be only that the shifter needs to be adjusted. Check Ogres Cave at the top of the screen to see if the procedure is in there.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000002||PBJ||11-25-2001||12:02 PM||||Hey Welcome,  It sounds like for some reason you were unable to release the clutch.  I would check you clutch master cylender fluid level, and correct it if required. If level is good it may be the clutch master cylender causing you the grief.||||reg||1
